\ A refcounted mutable map flows through a compiled word that duplicates the
\ operand slot (dup -> retain) and later discards the duplicate (drop ->
\ release). Under runtime-image AOT the word body is compiled, so the
\ generated code must release the dropped slot exactly as the interpreter
\ does. The check is that the AOT binary reproduces the interpreter result
\ without leaking or double-freeing the backing.

map-probe: ( m -- n ) [
  dup a: @get swap drop
] ;

M{ a: 1 b: 2 } map-probe .
